virglrenderer: do not tell the guest upstream's capability bit 19

What: capset bit 19 (capability_bits_v2) is no longer set. The macOS tap
(virglrenderer-macos-unified.patch) used it for its own
VIRGL_CAP_V2_CORE_PROFILE_ONLY, which no guest Mesa reads. Upstream gave the same
bit to VIRGL_CAP_V2_QUERY_FORMAT_MODIFIER (virglrenderer 652e8d8b "vrend: Support
tiled gbm allocation", Mesa c1ca2c89 "virgl: Support tiled gbm modifiers", in Mesa
26.3), which upstream sets only on a renderer with GBM and Venus interop. The
define now carries upstream's name; the tap's advertisement is gone.
Why: Mesa 26.3's virgl driver reads bit 19 as "the host answers the modifier
queries": it sends QUERY_GBM_FORMAT_MODIFIER (command 64) once per screen and
GET_PIPE_RESOURCE_LAYOUT (command 63) for every shared texture. This build has
no GBM, so command 63 is refused (EINVAL, upstream's non-GBM path) and the
context is lost: on Omarchy 4.0 VMs updated to Mesa 26.3.1 (Arch Linux ARM,
2026-11) Hyprland, Xwayland and quickshell lost their GL contexts at every start
("failed to dispatch GET_PIPE_RESOURCE_LAYOUT: 22", "Illegal command buffer
131135"). Without bit 19 Mesa 26.3 sends neither command, as on a GBM-less Linux
host. Mesa 26.2 and older never read bit 19. Command 64 is OmacVM's
VIRGL_CCMD_SET_RESET_STATUS_BUFFER here (virgl-context-loss-report.patch), sent
only by OmacVM's own guest Mesa build when bit 30 is set; upstream's
QUERY_GBM_FORMAT_MODIFIER has the same number, which a later virglrenderer pin
has to sort out (the patch would not apply over it).
Upstream status: not needed upstream (upstream never set bit 19 without GBM);
the tap's bit is a downstream choice, reported nowhere.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-caps-format-modifier.c (bit 19, bit 18 and 20..29 clear,
bit 30 set; GET_PIPE_RESOURCE_LAYOUT as Mesa 26.3 sends it and in malformed forms
is refused without a write to the guest's buffer; fails without this patch);
fuzz-regressions/seed-mesa263-layout; a 4.0 VM on Mesa 26.3.1 starts its desktop
with no lost context.
--- a/src/virgl_hw.h
+++ b/src/virgl_hw.h
@@ -629,7 +629,10 @@ enum virgl_formats {
 #define VIRGL_CAP_V2_MIRROR_CLAMP         (1u << 17)
 #define VIRGL_CAP_V2_RESOURCE_LAYOUT      (1u << 18)
 
-#define VIRGL_CAP_V2_CORE_PROFILE_ONLY    (1u << 19)
+/* Upstream's bit (virglrenderer 652e8d8b, Mesa 26.3): set only by a renderer with GBM and Venus
+ * interop. The macOS tap used it for CORE_PROFILE_ONLY, which no guest reads; with it set, Mesa
+ * 26.3 sent GET_PIPE_RESOURCE_LAYOUT for every shared texture and lost its context. */
+#define VIRGL_CAP_V2_QUERY_FORMAT_MODIFIER (1u << 19)
 /* VIRGL_CCMD_SET_RESET_STATUS_BUFFER is understood (OmacVM). */
 #define VIRGL_CAP_V2_RESET_STATUS_BUFFER  (1u << 30)
 /* virgl bind flags - these are compatible with mesa 10.5 gallium.
